    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nAfter updating cython in pkgsrc to 3.3.0, the build of lap 0.5.13 started failing with:\n```\nbuilding 'lap._lapjv' extension\nc++ -O2 -g -fstack-clash-protection -I/usr/pkg/include -I/usr/include -I/usr/pkg/include/python3.14 -g -I/usr/pkg/include -I/usr/include -I/usr/pkg/include/python3.14 -fPIC -I_lapjv_cpp -I/usr/pkg/lib/python3.14/site-packages/numpy/_core/include -Ilap -I/usr/pkg/include/python3.14 -c _lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.cpp -o build/temp.netbsd-11.99.7-amd64-cpython-314/_lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.o\n_lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.cpp: In function 'int __Pyx_PyObject_CompareFloatIntBoolLt(PyObject*, PyObject*)':\n_lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.cpp:12251:19: error: 'isfinite' was not declared in this scope; did you mean 'std::isfinite'?\n12251 |     if (unlikely(!isfinite(float_op1))) {\n      |                   ^~~~~~~~\n_lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.cpp:1504:43: note: in definition of macro 'unlikely'\n 1504 |   #define unlikely(x) __builtin_expect(!!(x), 0)\n      |                                           ^\nIn file included from /usr/include/g++/complex:44,\n                 from _lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.cpp:1544:\n/usr/include/g++/cmath:1142:5: note: 'std::isfinite' declared here\n 1142 |     isfinite(_Tp)\n      |     ^~~~~~~~\nerror: Command '['c++', '-O2', '-g', '-fstack-clash-protection', '-I/usr/pkg/include', '-I/usr/include', '-I/usr/pkg/include/python3.14', '-g', '-I/usr/pkg/include', '-I/usr/include', '-I/usr/pkg/include/python3.14', '-fPIC', '-I_lapjv_cpp', '-I/usr/pkg/lib/python3.14/site-packages/numpy/_core/include', '-Ilap', '-I/usr/pkg/include/python3.14', '-c', '_lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.cpp', '-o', 'build/temp.netbsd-11.99.7-amd64-cpython-314/_lapjv_cpp/_lapjv.o']' returned non-zero exit status 1.\n```\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\nTry building the 0.5.13 release of https://github.com/gatagat/lap using the pypi distfile.\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nBuild succeeds.\n\n### OS\n\nNetBSD\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.7\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
